{# How to keep the plan correct. The failed plan calls send steps as plain strings, a status
   other than pending or done, or no goal. A step has two statuses, pending and done. #}
Keeping the plan

{{ tool('update_plan') }} takes the goal and the whole list of steps. Each step has text and status, and a done step has a short note.

1. Send the whole list in every call, in order. A step that you leave out is no longer in the plan.
2. Give each step as an object with text and status. status is pending or done.
3. A step is pending until its work ends. Then send it as done with a note, giving the saved version and coverage for a dataset.
4. Keep the text of a step the same when only its status changes. The step then keeps its id.
5. A new goal starts a new plan.
6. {{ tool('update_plan') }} only keeps the plan. Write a report or another file with {{ tool('write_file') }}.

For an investigation, name the source scope, destination file and completion condition in each step.
Create the report with the first batch. Patch it after each small batch using verified citation handles.
Check the returned filename and version before moving on. Repair a rejected batch and retry the save.
Record missing evidence as unresolved when the source cannot establish the claim.
Keep missing evidence in the corresponding row. Deduplicate people when combining datasets.
A saved page or a TODO note cannot substitute for the extracted rows.

Example plan for a current and historical roster:
```json
{"goal":"Identify board members who held a qualifying office.","steps":[{"text":"Extract the current roster through its last entry into current-board.csv with membership citations.","status":"pending"},{"text":"Extract the former roster into former-board.csv with membership citations and known periods.","status":"pending"},{"text":"Check the saved candidates and record offices, evidence and unresolved cases in us-roles.csv.","status":"pending"},{"text":"Patch report.md after each batch with its membership and office evidence. Reconcile totals against the saved rows.","status":"pending"}]}
```
Add a historical source when you identify a specific coverage gap. Keep the step pending while that source has unread entries.
After a successful write, record the actual version. For example: “current-board.csv v2 covers the full current roster.”
